{"name":"Mantra","hex":"#dce2df","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mantra","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The hymn portions of the Vedas; any passage of these used as a prayer. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A phrase repeated to assist concentration during meditation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mantra"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mantra","blocks":[{"text":"A mantra or mantram is a sacred utterance, a numinous sound, syllable, word or phonemes, or group of words that practitioners believe to have religious, magical or spiritual powers. Etymologically derived from Sanskrit, the word \"mantra\" combines the roots \"man-\" and \"-tra\" ; consequently, a mantra can be understood as a mental tool designed to focus and control thought. Some mantras have a syntactic structure and literal meaning, while others do not."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Om_symbol.svg/330px-Om_symbol.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mantra","wikidata":"Q131510"},{"title":"Mantra (Jennie song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Mantra\" is a song by South Korean singer and rapper Jennie. It was released through Odd Atelier and Columbia Records on October 11, 2024, as the lead single from her debut studio album, Ruby (2025). It is Jennie's first release under her own label and her first solo single since departing YG Entertainment and Interscope Records as a solo artist in 2023. The song was written and composed by various contributors, including Jennie, Claudia Valentina, and Zikai, and was produced by El Guincho, Jelli Dorman, Jumpa, and Serban Cazan. It has been described as a dance-pop and Miami bass song that incorporates a heavy dose of R&B, with lyrics that celebrate girl power."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ad/Jennie_-_Mantra.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mantra_(Jennie_song)","wikidata":"Q130425894"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Carved-in-white-marble7.jpg/500px-Carved-in-white-marble7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Carved-in-white-marble7.jpg/500px-Carved-in-white-marble7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarved-in-white-marble7.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Tianjin_Temple_Sanskrit_Ranjana_Script.jpeg/500px-Tianjin_Temple_Sanskrit_Ranjana_Script.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Tianjin_Temple_Sanskrit_Ranjana_Script.jpeg/500px-Tianjin_Temple_Sanskrit_Ranjana_Script.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATianjin_Temple_Sanskrit_Ranjana_Script.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Kalachakra_Mandala_Samye_Ling.jpg/500px-Kalachakra_Mandala_Samye_Ling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Kalachakra_Mandala_Samye_Ling.jpg/500px-Kalachakra_Mandala_Samye_Ling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKalachakra_Mandala_Samye_Ling.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/2017_Woodstock_017_Hare_Kryszna.jpg/500px-2017_Woodstock_017_Hare_Kryszna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/2017_Woodstock_017_Hare_Kryszna.jpg/1280px-201